From 9b7e8f26b158d07825cd6c85295b56b76add297f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:58:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ci(tests): retry only the failed test ids once in-job; flaky
 ids get one Kanban card each [daveey]

run_tests_parallel.py retried a failing FILE: one flaky test in
test_run_agent.py cost another 320 s, and a test that flaked twice under
load turned the slice red, which meant a ~1 h whole-shard rerun (#38).
The retry now reruns only the node ids from pytest's short summary
(falling back to the whole file for collection errors/crashes). A pass
on retry stays FLAKY and is written to --flaky-report
(HERMES_TEST_FLAKY_REPORT); scripts/ci/flaky_kanban.py turns each id
into one deflake card (comments while open, a linked new card if it
flakes after close). A test that fails twice keeps the run red.

t_94f2c8ba
